# __title__

__description__

Built on [flutter_kit](https://github.com/bangdinh/flutter-kit) (`__kit_ref__`) — Feature-first
Clean Architecture + Riverpod 3.x. The kit provides the app shell, HTTP stack, storage, theme system
and shared widgets; this repo provides the environment, routes, features and product rules.

## Setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env.dev && cp .env.example .env.staging && cp .env.example .env.prod
$EDITOR .env.dev            # set API_BASE_URL per environment
make get && make gen
make ci                     # analyze + test
make run-dev
```

`.env.*` are gitignored — never commit them, and never commit the `env.g.dart` they generate
(envied obfuscates, it does not encrypt).

## Layout

```
lib/bootstrap.dart       app rules: KitConfig + provider overrides
lib/app/env/             environment resolution → KitConfig
lib/app/router/          GoRouter + route paths
lib/app/app.dart         brand palette + KitApp
lib/features/<name>/     data/ domain/ presentation/
```

## Add a feature

```bash
make feature NAME=profile   # scaffolds data/domain/presentation from the kit
make gen
```

Then follow the order in `.claude/skills/feature-flow/SKILL.md`: entity → repository contract →
fake → DTO → datasource → repository impl → provider → page → route → test.

## Commands

`make help` lists everything. The ones that matter: `make gen`, `make analyze`, `make test`,
`make ci`, `make run-dev`, `make feature NAME=<name>`.

## Upgrading the kit

Edit `ref:` in `pubspec.yaml`, then `make get && make gen && make ci`. Read the kit's `CHANGELOG.md`
first — pre-1.0, a minor bump can be breaking. Keep the bump in its own commit.

